# E2E Cucumber Conventions

## Feature File Structure

- One feature per file, scoped to a single user journey
- Use `Scenario` (not `Scenario Outline`) for distinct flows
- Each scenario should be independently runnable — include all prerequisites in `Given`

```gherkin
Feature: User Registration
    As a user
    I want to be able to register to the application
    So that I can add my income and get paid

    Scenario: Complete individual registration and reach the dashboard
        Given I am logged in and on the registration page
        When I fill in first name "E2E" and last name "Test"
        ...
        Then I should be on the individual dashboard
```

## Page Object Pattern (ADR 0001)

See [`docs/adr/0001-page-object-pattern.md`](../../docs/adr/0001-page-object-pattern.md) for the full decision record.

**All Playwright selectors and interactions must live in page object classes under `e2e/cucumber/pages/`.** Step definitions contain no selectors — only page object method calls and assertions.

### File structure

```
e2e/cucumber/
  pages/
    <name>.page.ts      ← selectors and interactions live here
  steps/
    <name>.steps.ts     ← page object calls + assertions only
```

### Page object contract

- Constructor receives a Playwright `Page` instance
- One `Page` instance shared across all page objects in `Before` hook
- Methods named after user actions, not selectors

```typescript
// pages/registration.page.ts
export class RegistrationPage {
  constructor(private page: Page) {}
  async fillFirstName(firstName: string) {
    await this.page.locator("#FirstName").fill(firstName);
  }
}

// steps/login.steps.ts  ✅ correct
When("I fill in first name {string} and last name {string}", async function (firstName, lastName) {
  await registrationPage.fillFirstName(firstName);
  await registrationPage.fillLastName(lastName);
});

// steps/login.steps.ts  ❌ wrong — selector in step file
When("I fill in first name {string} and last name {string}", async function (firstName, lastName) {
  await page.locator("#FirstName").fill(firstName);
});
```

## Step Definitions (`e2e/cucumber/steps/*.steps.ts`)

- Use `chromium` via Playwright; instantiate page objects in `Before`/`After` hooks
- `APP_URL` is `http://localhost:4200`
- Keycloak runs at `localhost:9000`; credentials are `e2e` / `s3cr3t`
- For file upload steps, reference fixtures from `e2e/cucumber/fixtures/`

## Registration Flow

After login, new users land on `/firstlogin`. Selectors are encapsulated in `RegistrationPage`:

| Field | Selector (in `registration.page.ts`) |
|---|---|
| First Name | `#FirstName` |
| Last Name | `#LastName` |
| Bank Account Name | `#bankAccountName` |
| Bank | `#bankCode` (select) |
| Bank Account Number | `#bankAccountNumber` |
| Phone | `#phone` |
| Slack Account | `#slackAccount` |
| User Type (role) | `#role` (select: `individual` or `corporate`) |
| Site | `#siteId` (select first non-empty option) |
| ID Card PDF | `input[type="file"]` — use `setInputFiles()` |

After submit with `role=individual` → redirected to `/individual`.

## Fixtures

Place test files in `e2e/cucumber/fixtures/`. Example: `test-idcard.pdf` for the ID card upload step.

## Running Tests

```bash
make e2e                        # run all scenarios
make e2e ARGS="--tags @tag"     # run tagged scenarios
```
